karr #33 is done: _request's params loop expands an ArrayRef value into one pair per element.

API::Docker::API::Images can drop its private workaround:

  sub get_all {
    my ($self, @names) = @_;
    @names = @{$names[0]} if @names == 1 && ref $names[0] eq 'ARRAY';
    croak 'At least one image name required' unless @names;
    return $self->client->get('/images/get', params => { names => \@names }, raw => 1);
  }

and _names_query goes with its comment block (currently lines 547-562).

The wire form is byte-identical, checked against the hand-built query for four inputs: 'alpine:3','registry:2' -> names=alpine:3&names=registry:2; 'my repo/img:1' -> names=my%20repo/img:1; 'a&b' -> names=a%26b; 'reg.example.com:5000/x/y:tag' unescaped throughout. So t/images_tar.t's 'get_all: names is a repeated query parameter' and 'get_all: the escaping keeps an image reference intact' carry over unchanged.

Images.pm was locked to another agent while the transport work ran, which is why this was not done in the same change.
